From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin Walsh <contact.me@thejustinwalsh.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 02:48:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] cuda: a quantized KV cache with a sparse mask decodes on the
 sparse MMA kernel

ggml_cuda_get_best_fattn_kernel sends a quantized K/V with one or two queries
(Ada and newer; one on older cards) to the vector kernel, which reads every
cell; only an f16 cache was checked for the sparse decode (the MMA kernel's
index-list gather, a mask with an n_kv_max hint). So Flash-Next's QSA layers
with the default q8_0 cache read the whole cache on every single-token decode
step and every MTP draft step: a cost linear in the context, and with the cache
in host-mapped memory a latency-bound walk over PCIe -- 4K decode 4.9 tok/s,
~35K 0.9 tok/s without MTP, against 21-25 with the cache on the card (the
Flash-Next gate's fit-kvmap-nomtp and probe-q8-cpu arms, 2026-09-30, n=1 each).

A quantized cache now takes the same sparse-decode test the f16 one does and,
when it holds, the MMA kernel -- which with the previous patch converts only
the selected cells to f16. GGML_CUDA_FA_SPARSE_QUANT=0 restores the vector
kernel.
---
 ggml/src/ggml-cuda/fattn.cu | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/fattn.cu b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/fattn.cu
index ad4d1df2..d1e7309f 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/fattn.cu
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/fattn.cu
@@ -538,6 +538,15 @@ static bool ggml_cuda_fattn_kv_type_supported(const ggml_type type) {
     }
 }
 
+// GGML_CUDA_FA_SPARSE_QUANT=0: a quantized cache's decode back on the vector kernel (every cell read)
+static bool ggml_cuda_fattn_sparse_quantized_enabled() {
+    static const bool on = [] {
+        const char * e = getenv("GGML_CUDA_FA_SPARSE_QUANT");
+        return !(e && e[0] == '0');
+    }();
+    return on;
+}
+
 static best_fattn_kernel ggml_cuda_get_best_fattn_kernel(const int device, const ggml_tensor * dst) {
 #ifndef FLASH_ATTN_AVAILABLE
     GGML_UNUSED(device); GGML_UNUSED(dst);
@@ -647,6 +656,14 @@ static best_fattn_kernel ggml_cuda_get_best_fattn_kernel(const int device, const
                     return BEST_FATTN_KERNEL_VEC;
                 }
             } else {
+                // a quantized cache with a sparse (n_kv_max) mask takes the sparse gather too: the vector kernel reads
+                // every cell, the MMA kernel only the selected ones (converted to f16 at those cells alone)
+                const bool sparse_decode = ggml_cuda_fattn_sparse_quantized_enabled() && gqa_opt_applies && gqa_ratio > 4 &&
+                    ggml_cuda_flash_attn_ext_mma_f16_may_use_sparse(K->ne[0], V->ne[0], 1, 8) &&
+                    ggml_cuda_flash_attn_ext_mma_f16_shall_use_sparse(cc, dst, 1, 8);
+                if (sparse_decode) {
+                    return BEST_FATTN_KERNEL_MMA_F16;
+                }
                 if (cc >= GGML_CUDA_CC_ADA_LOVELACE) {
                     if (Q->ne[1] <= 2) {
                         return BEST_FATTN_KERNEL_VEC;
